      <h1>Flamenco Guitar Gallery</h1>
      <h2 class="subtitle">Technique, emotion, and rhythm</h2>

      <p>This page celebrates the artistry of the <strong>flamenco guitar</strong>, where <em>compás</em>, percussive attack, and expressive melody meet in one instrument.</p>

      <hr />

      <h2>Signature Techniques</h2>

      <div class="gallery-grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>🎶 Rasgueado</h3>
          <p>A rapid strumming pattern that delivers the fiery, aggressive character associated with flamenco.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Fast attack</li>
            <li>Bright texture</li>
            <li>High energy</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card accent-card">
          <h3>🎼 Tremolo</h3>
          <p>A sustained, repeating pattern that creates a lyrical and atmospheric quality in the melody.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Continuous shimmer</li>
            <li>Emotional tone</li>
            <li>Long sustained notes</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>🥁 Golpe</h3>
          <p>Percussive taps on the guitar body add rhythmic punch and the unmistakable flamenco feel.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Rhythmic accent</li>
            <li>Body percussion</li>
            <li>Dynamic drive</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <hr />

      <h2>Flamenco Form Examples</h2>

      <ol>
        <li><strong>Soleares</strong> – soulful and meditative</li>
        <li><strong>Bulerías</strong> – energetic and lively</li>
        <li><strong>Tangos</strong> – elegant and expressive</li>
        <li><strong>Fandangos</strong> – warm and lyrical</li>
      </ol>

